   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div>Is there a general way of keeping multiple similar models objects in a vector (like in C#)?</div><div>This, to be also applied for predictions as well.</div><div>Something like </div><div><br></div><div>for(i in 1:100) {</div><div><a href=\"http://data.bs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://data.bs&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497419282000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QNGNWEVLZmRrCvSwgwTEP\">data.bs</a> = bootstrap(data)</div><div>ModelsVector[i] = Model (Response~., <a href=\"http://data.bs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://data.bs&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497419282000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QNGNWEVLZmRrCvSwgwTEP\">data.bs</a>,...)</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
