  {
   "id": "E74plNuL4hIJ",
   "from": "Liad Shekel",
   "author": "0b2ad4fc9d8ed8eb",
   "date": "2015-03-15T10:26:02Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Israel RUG] Save a vector of model objects",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">You can use any R object to replace lm1 (the lm object).</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">list_of_models &lt;- vector(&quot;list&quot;, 100) </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">​for (i in 1:100){</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">lm1 &lt;- lm(y ~ x, subset = sample( ...whatever... ) )</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">list_of_models[i] &lt;- lm1<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">}​<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">Then, you can use sapply to create lists based on the lm object):<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">list_of_models %&gt;% sapply(function(x) x$fitted )<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">or <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">list_of_models %&gt;% sapply(function(x) predict(x) )<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">[[equivalent to sapply(list_of_models, function(x) predict(x) )]]</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, Mar 15, 2015 at 11:52 AM, eitan lifshits <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">eita...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
